      "side": 1,
      "message": "the basic problem is in\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/drivers/gpio/gpio_emul.c;l\u003d271\n`gpio_emul_pend_interrupt()`\n\nwhich calls the interrupt handler via `gpio_fire_callbacks()`,\nbut does not update `values`, its notion of the state of input pins.\nthis means that if the interrupt handler clears a level-triggered\ninterrupt source by changing the state of the input pin,\nthe loop will run forever.\n\ni changed the logic use `drv_data-\u003einput_vals` instead and that fixes\nthe problem for this unit test but breaks `drivers/drivers.usbc_power_contract`\ndue to a timeout.\nthat\u0027s the only one of the 440+ tests that would be affected...\ni\u0027m willing to bet the failure is due to a dependency on the original\nquirky behavior rather than a new bug.",
